Introduction of different R files:
The whole dataset is organized with this workflow:
First, use DataCleaningAndIntegration.R to organize existing datasets and select columns; then, use PairwiseMerge.R to merge between different datasets (among DocGraph, OpenPayment and Medicare D) and NPIHRRMapping.R to map NPI to HRR.
Afterwards, use DescriptiveAnalysis.R to understand the basics and NetworkPaymentAnalysis.R to conduct correlation analysis.

For additional changes: 
Use AddAdditionalColumns.R to add or remove information.

Other than that:
HypothesisAssistance.R is to select individual cases and ForTestingUse.R is not active now.

Data involved in the whole workflow:
DocGraph, Openpayments (now general payment only, should include research payment later), and Medicare D from 2015 till 2018; NPPES to map NPI to HRR and specialty.

Notice:
Data files are big so it is recommended to only include necessary columns whenever needed.
This GitHub file only includes Code. Data should be put in a seperate \Data folder in parallel to \Code.
